      ribbon.xml is intentionally NOT copied to the build output (and
      therefore NOT included in the MSI content list). It ships embedded
      in the assembly via Properties\Resources.resx (ResXFileRef), which
      is the canonical end-user path. Dropping the on-disk copy closes
      bug 13.1 followup (2026-05-13 evening): see
      .local/docs/bugs/msi-ribbon-stale-on-upgrade.md for the full story.
      Devs who want a hot-edit copy must explicitly drop a sibling
      ribbon.override.xml next to the DLL - the on-disk lookup in
      LanguageRegistry.Initialise / AddIn.LoadRibbon now uses that name.
    -->
    <None Include="ribbon.xml">
